<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110666" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φθέγ-μα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, τό</span> (written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φθέγγμα</span></b>  in late Inscrr., <i><span class="en">
			<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
			1002
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			1003
		</span></i>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sound of the voice,
				voice,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				8.31
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				588
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1623
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				319
			</span></i> (anap.), etc.; periphr. of a person, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ φθέγμ᾽ ἀναιδές,</span> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ
				φθεγξάμενε ἀναιδῆ,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				863
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Aj.</u>
				14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>El.</u>
				1225
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>language, speech,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				354
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>c.</b>
			<i>saying, word, utterance,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>OC</u>
				1177
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				616a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Wi.</u>
				1.11
			</span></i>: pl., <i>accents, words,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				655a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Polyzel.
				12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of other
			sounds, as of birds, <i>cries,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				747
			</span></i>; of a bull, <i>roaring,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				1215
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βροντᾶς φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					4.198
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυείας φ.</span> the
			<i>grinding</i> of the mortar, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				235
			</span></i>; of <i>musical notes,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Av.</u>
				683
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				812d
			</span></i>; of the nightingale's <i>song,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				204
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				223
			</span></i>.</div>
